                <pb facs="0395" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg291"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 224.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum.</hi></head>
                <p>France absolutely prohibited the importation of American pork, February 18, 1881,
                    being the first European nation, with the exception of Italy (February 20,
                    1879), to do so.</p>
                <p>Germany had, 8 months before (June 25, 1880), prohibited the importation of
                    sausages and prepared sausage meat, but not of hams and bacon.</p>
                <p>Following the example of France, Austria-Hungary prohibited American pork, March
                    10, 1881; Turkey, June 3, 1882; Germany, March 6, 1883; Greece, April 7, 19,
                    1883.</p>
            </div>
